IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ta-nouns`
IMPORT `ta-logic`

-- Terrorism Act 2000, Part III (Terrorist Property), section 14 -- layer 1.
-- Written from the deposited text alone.  What this module answers: JUST TRUE where a limb is met; NOTHING where the text
-- lists without closing the list ("includes") and the case falls outside the list.  No branch here answers JUST FALSE:
-- every limb of s 14(1) rests on a term that s 14(2) says "includes" more, so a case that meets no limb is outside what
-- the text lists, and the text does not say it is not terrorist property (NOTES.md, fork F1 and Marginal readings M3).
-- "For the purposes of terrorism" is section 1 of the Act and "proscribed organisation" is Part II; neither is among the
-- sources, so each is a fact the caller states (see ta-nouns.l4).

§ `Part III Terrorist Property -- Interpretation`
§§ `s 14 Terrorist property`

-- src:8 | (2) In subsection (1)—
-- src:9 | (a) a reference to proceeds of an act includes a reference to any property which wholly or partly, and directly or indirectly, represents the proceeds of the act (including payments or other rewards in connection with its commission), and
@ref s 14(2)(a) (src:8-9)
GIVEN `the facts about the act` IS A `Proceeds facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(2)(a) the property is proceeds of the act` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts about the act`'s `it is the proceeds of the act`
           OR `the facts about the act`'s `it represents the proceeds of the act, wholly or partly, directly or indirectly`
           OR `the facts about the act`'s `it is a payment or other reward in connection with the act's commission`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a reference to any property which wholly or partly, and directly or indirectly, represents the proceeds of the act"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:10 | (b) the reference to an organisation’s resources includes a reference to any money or other property which is applied or made available, or is to be applied or made available, for use by the organisation.
@ref s 14(2)(b) (src:10)
GIVEN `applied or made available, or to be applied or made available, for use by the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(2)(b) the property is among the organisation's resources` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `applied or made available, or to be applied or made available, for use by the organisation`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes a reference to any money or other property which is applied or made available, or is to be applied or made available, for use by the organisation"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:4 | (1) In this Act “terrorist property” means—
-- src:5 | (a) money or other property which is likely to be used for the purposes of terrorism (including any resources of a proscribed organisation),
@ref s 14(1)(a) (src:4-5)
GIVEN `the facts about the property` IS A `Property facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(1)(a) the property is likely to be used for the purposes of terrorism, or is a proscribed organisation's resources` IS
    `the disjunction` likely `or else` resources
    WHERE
        -- the caller's judgment that it is likely to be used is a plain fact; s 14(2)(b) answers JUST TRUE or NOTHING, so this answers JUST TRUE or NOTHING
        likely MEANS `the fact` (`the facts about the property`'s `likely to be used for the purposes of terrorism`)
        resources MEANS `s 14(2)(b) the property is among the organisation's resources` (`the facts about the property`'s `applied or made available, or to be applied or made available, for use by a proscribed organisation`)

-- src:6 | (b) proceeds of the commission of acts of terrorism, and
@ref s 14(1)(b) (src:6)
GIVEN `the facts about the property` IS A `Property facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(1)(b) the property is proceeds of the commission of acts of terrorism` IS
    `s 14(2)(a) the property is proceeds of the act` (`the facts about the property`'s `proceeds of the commission of acts of terrorism`)

-- src:7 | (c) proceeds of acts carried out for the purposes of terrorism.
@ref s 14(1)(c) (src:7)
GIVEN `the facts about the property` IS A `Property facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(1)(c) the property is proceeds of acts carried out for the purposes of terrorism` IS
    `s 14(2)(a) the property is proceeds of the act` (`the facts about the property`'s `proceeds of acts carried out for the purposes of terrorism`)

-- src:4 | (1) In this Act “terrorist property” means—
-- src:5 | (a) money or other property which is likely to be used for the purposes of terrorism (including any resources of a proscribed organisation),
-- src:6 | (b) proceeds of the commission of acts of terrorism, and
-- src:7 | (c) proceeds of acts carried out for the purposes of terrorism.
@ref s 14(1) (src:4-7)
GIVEN `the facts about the property` IS A `Property facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(1) the property is terrorist property` IS
    BRANCH
        IF limbA EQUALS JUST TRUE OR limbB EQUALS JUST TRUE OR limbC EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Act “terrorist property” means—" (a definition that says "means" is closed; s 14(2) begins "In subsection (1)" and extends only the two items it names, "proceeds of an act" and "an organisation’s resources", which the limbs already consult, so property that fits no limb is outside the definition: fork F1, reading (a))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        limbA MEANS `s 14(1)(a) the property is likely to be used for the purposes of terrorism, or is a proscribed organisation's resources` `the facts about the property`
        limbB MEANS `s 14(1)(b) the property is proceeds of the commission of acts of terrorism` `the facts about the property`
        limbC MEANS `s 14(1)(c) the property is proceeds of acts carried out for the purposes of terrorism` `the facts about the property`
